gHr(){return"What is stored"},
gHq(){return"Events, routines, categories, templates, sounds, proofs and settings are stored only on this device.\n\nOn Windows, Android, macOS and iOS they live in the app storage. On the web they live in the browser\u2019s local storage (localStorage). Dowit does not use cookies."},
gHp(){return"What Dowit does not do"},
gHo(){return"It does not collect your data for itself or for third parties.\nIt does not transmit the events, routines or settings you create.\nIt does not use analytics, telemetry, ads or in-app purchases.\nIt does not sell or share data.\nGitHub only publishes and hosts the app files. It is not a backend for your data."},
gHl(){return"Import, export and delete"},
gHk(){return"You can export and import a .dowit file by hand. You can also delete all local data from Settings."},
gHn(){return"Network"},
gHm(){return"The installable versions do not need the Internet once downloaded, except for dictation in search. That microphone uses the system speech recognizer: Dowit does not receive or store the audio, and the phrase may leave the device for the speech service on Windows, Android, iPhone or Mac. There is no microphone on the web. On Android, turning on the microphone can ask for permission for nearby devices and mention their position. That wording is the Bluetooth permission, in case recognition uses a headset. Dowit does not get the phone's location and does not search for devices. The web version is downloaded from GitHub Pages; that does not send your events.\n\nIf a text shows a character that the bundled fonts do not cover, for example an emoji, Flutter Web may request a fallback font from Google Fonts. That request does not include your data."},
