gEE(){return"In the Home filter you can check or uncheck categories: an event is hidden when it has an unchecked one. Mute is not the same: it mutes even if the event has other categories and also removes its alerts."},
gDu(){return"Create an event"},
gDs(){return"Tap the circle to pick the icon, type the title and move the color bar: the card below updates live."},
gDt(){return"The title can be left empty. The color paints the card, the icon and the notifications."},
gEi(){return"Priority"},
gEe(){return"Priority goes from 0 to 10 and sorts the list: urgent ones first."},
gEf(){return"Drag it: the number travels with your finger and settles when you release."},
gEt(){return"Simple schedule"},
gEr(){return"On the left, the start. On the right, the end, with its switches: turn one on and its wheel becomes active. The sentence below describes how the event looks with your choices."},
gEs(){return"\u2022 End time only: it repeats every day in that time window.\n\u2022 End date and time: the same daily window until that day.\n\u2022 No end: it stays active indefinitely."},
gDj(){return"The calendar"},
gDi(){return"\u2022 One tap marks the start; the second tap marks the end. Tapping the same day again clears the end.\n\u2022 Drag from one day to another: you pick the range in one go.\n\u2022 Month and year slide like the wheels.\n\u2022 Press and hold an arrow and the drag keeps moving through months.\nThis calendar is real: try it."},
gDo(){return"The range clock"},
gDn(){return"\u2022 One tap = start; two taps = end.\n\u2022 Drag a hand to adjust that time.\n\u2022 Slide the arc: you move both times without changing the duration.\n\u2022 The middle button swaps start and end.\n\u2022 22:00 to 04:00 crosses midnight: those are different days.\nThis clock is real: try it."},
gEO(){return"Weekly schedule"},
gEN(){return"You mark the days of the week and a single time window for all days that are on.\nIf the schedule crosses midnight (e.g. 22:00 to 02:00), the event runs from 22:00 to 23:59 and continues from 00:00 to 02:00."},
gEc(){return"Per-day schedule"},
gEb(){return"Each day has its own times and its own switch.\nIf the schedule crosses midnight (e.g. 22:00 to 02:00), the event runs from 22:00 to 23:59 and continues from 00:00 to 02:00."},
gDa(){return"The event screen"},
gD9(){return'Tap a card and this screen opens: the state at the top and the actions at the bottom (Postpone, Complete, Cancel, Edit, "Not now").'},
gD8(){return"Event screen with the state at the top and the Postpone, Complete, Cancel, Edit and Not now actions at the bottom."},
gEw(){return"No sound, Notification or Alarm"},
gEu(){return"Each circle shows one mode from the sound menu, with what it does beside it. In the form, the circle cycles through the three."},
gEv(){return"Next to the menu you pick the sound from your library. No sound never notifies."},
gEl(){return"Reminders"},
gEk(){return'Remind every: notifies several times while the event is active. From 06:00 to 12:00 with "every 1 hour" it sounds at 07:00, 08:00, 09:00, 10:00 and 11:00.\nPick the interval:'},
gDf(){return"Advance alerts"},
gDe(){return"An advance alert notifies a while before each start, with an optional message for the notification.\nAdd several: if two are exactly the same, the app tells you it only keeps the first one."},
gEo(){return"Repeat"},
gEm(){return"The Repeat switch on the form turns the event into a routine: you pick how often to repeat and when to stop."},
gEn(){return"This creates a routine in the Routines tab: occurrences are generated on their own, the first action you take releases the next one, and pausing freezes generation."},
gEL(){return"Templates"},
gEJ(){return'A template is a mold: icon, color, priority, sound, schedule and tasks ready to create events faster.\nThey are created from the + button on the main list: press and hold it and tap "Create template", the label that appears in the corner.\nYou can also base one on an event you already have: open it in the form and tap the bookmark button in the top-right corner ("Save as template").'},
gEK(){return"Each pill has the trash can to delete it and the pencil that opens its editor."},
gEy(){return"Sounds"},
gEx(){return"The Sounds tab in Manage stores your tones: try them with \u25b6, delete with the trash can, and rename by tapping the name.\nIf you delete one that an event uses, that event reverts to Default."},
